sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Baculites compressus at 94.16 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 83.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Cell-frame Schnakenberg system (a=0.10, b=0.90, r=9.2 just above r_c≈8.568) is calibrated so k_c = 2π/94.16 µm. Numeric growth rates track the analytic dispersion with Pearson r = 0.99966 and RMSE = 0.00884 per τ. Equal diffusion decays (σ≈−0.77). The fastest mode is 96.54 µm, not forced onto 94.16. Aperture factor χ is the series parameter: Placenticeras 141.24 µm, Baculites 94.16 µm at 73.5 Ma, Nipponites 62.15 µm. The flank GIF is a band-limited suture packet on a capsule, compared with Kevmin's CC BY-SA polished section. The comparison figure prints orientation KS, radial-FFT r, and coherency. The eigenmode step is still 0.12 of the diffusion stability bound (RMSE 0.00884 per τ). Overall 83.3/100 (faithfulness 82.0, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8f0ebbb7583b60dab933158a86eda8e291baab3e; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-baculites-compressus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8f0ebbb7583b60dab933158a86eda8e291baab3e, image/png, 359866 B, 1512×888 px, artifact_sha256 11bd13ddcc65dc8a7d1dfcc65fe246d773d1d497dc22e37d3fe1465b60855fa7 (sha256 11bd13ddcc65dc8a7d1dfcc65fe246d773d1d497dc22e37d3fe1465b60855fa7), spec_fingerprint 987c95abfd36be5a754c6bd9b1cc8b19b4c29acfc2ed8558194b88bb00b620d6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 987c95abfd36be5a754c6bd9b1cc8b19b4c29acfc2ed8558194b88bb00b620d6; artifact_sha256: 11bd13ddcc65dc8a7d1dfcc65fe246d773d1d497dc22e37d3fe1465b60855fa7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/baculites_compressus_specimen.jpg=b4eabd655977c5ee..., datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=1e794dec0e5bf0ec..., datasets/baculites_compressus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=03254933877482eb...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and the inhibitor-long-range instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) trimolecular steady state u0=a+b, v0=b/(a+b)^2. | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987): mollusc pigment records a mantle-edge reaction-diffusion system. | G. C. C. (1892): Baculites compressus has a coiled early stage before the orthoconic shaft. | Fatherree, Harries & Quinn (1998): B. compressus in the upper Campanian Pierre Shale of South Dakota.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u solved so the k_c formula returns λ_c = 94.16 µm at r = 9.2 and χ = 1. | Numeric σ(k) from a periodic eigenmode integrator, and the equal-diffusion ablation. | χ readout 3/2 and 6215/9416 for the predecessor and successor. | Flank mode packet and foreground segmentation of the Kevmin photograph.; transfer_boundary: The photograph is a Bearpaw Formation section; the age anchor 73.5 Ma is the Pierre Shale zone. | Shell-pigment RD is transferred from gastropod models to an ammonite mantle.; does_not_claim: 94.16 µm was not measured on the photograph. | χ for Placenticeras and Nipponites is not a fossil pigment measurement. | The Wikimedia caption age of 100 Ma is not used. | The flank GIF is not a 2D integration of the PDE on the shell mesh.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Tighten the eigenmode timestep from 0.12 to 0.06 of the explicit diffusion bound and report the new dispersion RMSE against the Pass-1 value 0.00884.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Put the Bearpaw-versus-Pierre-Shale transfer and the 94.16 µm versus 2.7 cm distinction in the comparison-figure caption, not only in the reference JSON.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Keep the diffusion-sweep panel labeled as a local probe after the timestep change, so the dispersion curve remains the independent fit.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.833"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

